    "is_private": false,
    "title": "Reading Macondo in Caribeantillean / Leyendo a Macondo en Caribe Antillano ",
    "description": "What about reading Gabo (Gabriel García Márquez) in Caribbean?  I want to offer a Caribbean/antillean reading of GGM stories, embracing everything about it that may seem broken, imperfect, and out of joint (even to me).  Intentionally, I’m trying to avoid self-correction as I read, allowing myself to move beyond rigid self-awareness and into a more spontaneous mode of reading, preserving my aspirations, consonant weakening, elisions, assimilations, vowel reductions, variations in rhotic and lateral sounds, intonation, rhythm, pauses, hesitations, and other spontaneous features of my Caribbean/antillean speech. I want to let these features as apparent defects emerge naturally, without imposing an idealized standard of pronunciation on my voice. That is why this is reading Gabo in the Caribbean and as a Caribbean.  \n\n",
    "language": "en",
